      "writtenOn": "2025-09-12T19:39:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It occured to me to check the auto-downloading behavior of npx. I think we only want to use packages we\u0027ve already installed from `npm ci`, so really we should pass `--no`, especially because:\n\n\u003e If any requested packages are not present in the local project\ndependencies, then a prompt is printed, which can be suppressed by\nproviding either --yes or --no. **When standard input is not a TTY or a\nCI environment is detected, --yes is assumed.** The requested packages\nare installed to a folder in the npm cache, which is added to the PATH\nenvironment variable in the executed process.\n\nfrom `npm help exec`\n\nNot sure if we should pass it here or if we `run-cts` should pass it (or both). Perhaps even better if at some point we can make `run-cts` not use npx...",
      "revId": "25ff842b56a449b56b28ca08a4877fc7ad4b5a14",
